    "body": "I've tested some mutations related to test coverage for PSBT unknown field merging and discovered an inconsistency.\n<details>\n\nIf line 71 of `psbt.cpp` \"`unknown.insert(psbt.unknown.begin(), psbt.unknown.end());`\"  (inside `bool PartiallySignedTransaction::Merge(const PartiallySignedTransaction& psbt)` function) is removed then, the expected test fails: *\"Test that combining PSBTs preserves unknown fields with the same and with distinct values per map.\"*\n\nIf line 434 of `psbt.cpp` \"`unknown.insert(input.unknown.begin(), input.unknown.end());`\" (inside `bool PSBTInput::Merge(const PSBTInput& input)` function), is removed, a different unexpected test fails: \"*Test that unknown values are just passed through*\".\n\nIf line 537 of `psbt.cpp` \"`unknown.insert(output.unknown.begin(), output.unknown.end());`\" (inside `bool PSBTOutput::Merge(const PSBTOutput& output)` function), is removed, the expected test fails: \"*Test that combining PSBTs preserves unknown fields with the same and with distinct values per map.*\".\n</details>\n\nThis PR solves this inconsistency.\nThe old code did 3 different things:\n1. Test the pass-through of unknown values for `walletprocesspsbt`.\n2. Combine two v0 PSBTs with different unknown input keys and check that both keys survive.\n3. Combine implicit v0 PSBT with explicit v0 and check that both keys survive.\n\nCase 2 is already fully covered by the existing `test_combinepsbt_preseves_unknown_fields` so keeping it is redundant and misleading.\n\nCommit 40eba5eb20ba0041a6328ba3482fcc26ddbe0185 moves the old code into a new method called `test_unknown_fields_passthrough` and commit dd18f9f4d582ce2b91617ce8b56c3aec26bf5a47 removes the redundant code of Case 2 and moves Case 3 inside `test_combinepsbt_preserves_unknown_fields`.",
